 oral contraceptive pills (risk for thromboembolic events)", "Daily alcohol consumption (5 standard drinks) (contributing to systemic risk)"], "excluded_candidates": ["Acute cholecystitis: Unlikely due to absence of fever, jaundice, or biliary colic pattern", "Exercise-induced musculoskeletal injury: Could explain pain exacerbation but insufficient to explain shock", "Alcohol-induced acute pancreatitis: Atypical for right upper quadrant localization and shock presentation", "Gastritis/peptic ulcer disease: Would not typically cause hemodynamic instability", "Ovarian torsion: Low priority due to lack of pelvic exam findings or adnexal tenderness"], "alarm_features": ["Hypotension with tachycardia (shock)", "Severe localized right upper quadrant pain (potential intra-abdominal source)", "Unprotected sexual activity with prior gonococcal infection (risk for pelvic sepsis)", "Oral contraceptive use (thromboembolic risk factor for Budd-Chiari syndrome)"]}, "branches": {"B1": {"id": "B1", "label": "Gynecologic / Pelvic Source of Shock", "parent": "ROOT", "level": 1, "status": "live", "prior": 0.4761904761904762, "posterior": 0.3558718861209964, "danger": 1.0, "actionability": 0.0, "explanatory_coverage": 0.0, "expand_score": 0.0, "evidence_for": [], "evidence_against": ["Weight loss for fitness shows strong exclusion of gynecologic/pelvic shock (B1) as a definitive mechanism."], "unresolved_questions": [], "children": [], "closure_reason": "", "turn_cost_to_refine": 1.5, "diagnosis_commitment_gain": 0.5, "interrupt_relevance": 1.0, "level_role": "family", "classification_axis": "anatomy", "representative_diseases": []}, "B2": {"id": "B2", "label": "Hepatic / Hepatobiliary Vascular Source of Shock", "parent": "ROOT", "level": 1, "status": "live", "prior": 0.2857142857142857, "posterior": 0.4270462633451957, "danger": 1.0, "actionability": 0.0, "explanatory_coverage": 0.0, "expand_score": 0.0, "evidence_for": ["Hypercoagulable state (OCP + alcohol) weakly supports Budd-Chia