ort Budd-Chiari syndrome as the shock mechanism despite absent hepatomegaly/ascites?", "summary": "Hypercoagulable state (OCP + alcohol) weakly supports Budd-Chiari syndrome (B2) as a risk factor, but lack of hepatomegaly/ascites reduces this support."}, {"t": 3, "type": "ANALYZE_VIGNETTE", "content": "Does the right upper quadrant pain pattern and absence of biliary colic strongly indicate biliary obstruction with shock despite missing fever/jaundice?", "summary": "RUQ pain without typical biliary colic weakly supports biliary obstruction (B3), but missing fever/jaundice undermines this pattern."}, {"t": 3, "type": "ANALYZE_VIGNETTE", "content": "Does the absence of hepatomegaly, ascites, and jaundice definitively rule out Budd-Chiari syndrome as a life-threatening cause of shock?", "summary": "Lack of hepatomegaly/ascites weakly argues against Budd-Chiari (B2), though hypotension persists."}, {"t": 3, "type": "ANALYZE_VIGNETTE", "content": "Does the complete absence of fever, jaundice, and biliary colic patterns definitively rule out biliary obstruction as a shock mechanism?", "summary": "Absence of fever/jaundice/colic moderately argues against biliary obstruction (B3) as a shock cause."}, {"t": 3, "type": "ANALYZE_VIGNETTE", "content": "What evidence is MOST INCONSISTENT with Gynecologic / Pelvic Source of Shock? Identify the single strongest finding that argues against this diagnosis.", "summary": "Weight loss for fitness shows strong exclusion of gynecologic/pelvic shock (B1) as a definitive mechanism."}], "differential_history": [{"top": [["B1", 0.476], ["B2", 0.286], ["B1.2", 0.212]]}, {"top": [["B1", 0.592], ["B1.3", 0.345], ["B1.2", 0.182]]}], "deliberation": {}, "interrupt": {"active": true, "reason": "Patient exhibits hypotension (80/40 mmHg) and tachycardia (110 bpm) indicating major haemodynamic instability (shock). Severe localized right upper quadrant pain with diffuse tenderness suggests potential intra-abdominal source requiring immediate stabilization.", "required_actions": ["Continue IV fluid resuscitation", "Monitor for response to fluids", "Consider vasopressor support if hypotension persists", "Order lactate level and CBC to assess shock severity", "Prepare for emergent imaging (FAST exam or CT) if hemodynamic stability achieved"]}, "termination": {"ready_to_stop": false, "termination_type": "continue", "reason": "No branch meets posterior >=0.75 confirmation threshold. Dangerous alternatives (B1.2: PID, B2: Budd-Chiari, B3: biliary obstruction) remain unresolved with posterior >=0.10. Emergency override requires stabilization but needs further diagnostic clarification before management can be determined."}, "turn_budget_used": 2, "estimated_remaining_value": 0.52, "max_turn_budget": 5, "latest_action_type": "ANALYZE_VIGNETTE", "diagnosis_readiness_score": 0.34524942961383337, "benchmark_output_ready": false, "static_question": "Which of the following is the most likely the diagnosis?", "static_options": [{"id": "A", "description": "Ectopic implantation of a blastocyst"}, {"id": "B", "description": "Inflammation of the pancreas"}, {"id": "C", "description": "Obstruction of blood flow through the hepatic vein"}, {"id": "D", "description": "Obstruction of the common bile duct by radio-opaque stones"}, {"id": "E", "description": "Vascular ectasia within the liver"}], "seen_evidence_ids": [], "seen_evidence_phenotypes": "{'Biliary tract obstruction', 'gas', 'Cholangitis', 'acute pancreatitis', 'shock', 'epigastric pain'}", "mode_policy": {"benchmark_purity": true, "allow_external_knowledge": true}, "answer_option_mapping": {}, "root_revision_needed": true, "max_tree_depth": 3, "reasoning_ledger": {"anchor": {"hypothesis": "B1", "t": 0, "posterior_at_anchor": 0.476}, "leader": {"branch_id": "B2", "label": "Hepatic / Hepatobiliary Vascular Source of Shock", "posterior": 0.427, "leading_since_t": 0, "n_revisions": 0}, "leader_evidence": {"confirming": 1, "disconfirming": 1, "last_disconfirming_digest": "Lack of